Subject: [PATCH] mm: use the HG8245 low-memory watermark policy from boot

On this 50 MiB target a single pageblock boost can reserve 8 MiB while
the kernel is unpacking the initramfs. Userspace sysctl runs too late.
Keep the normal low-memory watermarks and the writable sysctl.

--- a/mm/page_alloc.c
+++ b/mm/page_alloc.c
@@ -313,7 +313,7 @@
 
 int min_free_kbytes = 1024;
 int user_min_free_kbytes = -1;
-static int watermark_boost_factor __read_mostly = 15000;
+static int watermark_boost_factor __read_mostly;
 static int watermark_scale_factor = 10;
 
 /* movable_zone is the "real" zone pages in ZONE_MOVABLE are taken from */
